---
import Cost from '../components/Cost.astro'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { GEM_PACKS, INVITES, STARTER_PACK, art, duration, game, num, strongholds, url } from '../lib/game'

const campaignGems = strongholds.reduce((s, x) => s + (x.rewards[2].gems ?? 0), 0)
const achievementGems = game.achievements.reduce((s, a) => s + a.tiers.reduce((x, t) => x + t.gems, 0), 0)
---

<Layout title="Gems" description="Gems in Horizon: how to earn them, what they buy, the gem packs and the Starter Pack, gifts for friends and invite rewards." crumbs={[['Wiki', ''], ['Gems', 'gems/']]}>
  <div class="intro">
    <img src={art('icons/gems.webp')} alt="" width="84" height="84" />
    <div>
      <h1>Gems</h1>
      <p class="lede">The kingdom's rubies. They hurry things along — they never buy what can't be won by playing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Earning gems</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your first day:</strong> every new kingdom starts with 250 gems, and Captain Maren's guide ends with 250 more.</li>
    <li><strong>Strongholds:</strong> the third star of every stronghold pays gems — {num(campaignGems)} across all {strongholds.length}. <a href={url('strongholds/')}>See them</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Achievements:</strong> {num(achievementGems)} gems across all tiers. <a href={url('ranks/#achievements')}>See them</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The daily gift:</strong> come back every day — days 3, 6 and 7 of the week's streak pay gems. <a href="#daily">See the gifts</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>The steward's orders:</strong> three small tasks a day, with gems and gold for each.</li>
    <li><strong>Clearing the land:</strong> trees, bushes and rocks sometimes hide a gem or two.</li>
    <li><strong>Friends:</strong> invite rewards and gifts, below.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What gems buy</h2>
  <p>
    Mostly time: finishing a building, an upgrade, training or research at once. The longer the wait, the more it costs — but less per hour the longer it is.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Time left</th>
          {game.gemsForTime.map((g) => <th class="num">{duration(g.seconds)}</th>)}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Gems to finish now</td>
          {game.gemsForTime.map((g) => <td class="num">{num(g.gems)}</td>)}
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Gems also build <strong>more houses</strong> — each house is home to one more villager, so one more thing can be built at once:{' '}
    {game.houses.gemPrice.map((g, i) => `house ${i + 1}: ${g ? `${num(g)} gems` : 'free'}`).join(', ')} — {game.houses.max} at most. And they wake <a href={url('lord/')}>the Lord</a> early after a hard battle.
  </p>

  <h2>Gem packs</h2>
  <p>Prices are set by the App Store and Google Play in your own currency. Watch for gem-pack events: while one is on, every gem pack pays a bonus share of gems on top.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    {
      GEM_PACKS.map((p) => (
        <div class="card pack">
          <img src={art('icons/gems.webp')} alt="" width="48" height="48" />
          <h3>{p.name}</h3>
          <p class="display" style="font-size: 26px; color: var(--walnut)">{num(p.gems)} gems</p>
          <p class="small">Can be sent as a gift</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
    <div class="card pack starter">
      <img src={art('icons/shop.webp')} alt="" width="48" height="48" />
      <h3>{STARTER_PACK.name}</h3>
      <p class="display" style="font-size: 26px; color: var(--walnut)">{num(STARTER_PACK.gems)} gems</p>
      <p class="small">plus <Cost cost={STARTER_PACK.goods} /></p>
      <p class="small">Once per store account</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="daily">The daily gift</h2>
  <p>
    Tap <strong>Daily</strong> on the home screen once a day for a chest from the treasurer. Seven days make a streak, and every day of it pays more; miss a day and the streak
    starts again from day 1. The goods grow with your Keep (the gems don't). A new day begins at midnight UTC.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Day</th>
          <th>Keep 1</th>
          <th>Keep 3</th>
          <th>Keep 6</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          game.dailyGift['1'].map((_, d) => (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <strong>Day {d + 1}</strong>
              </td>
              {(['1', '3', '6'] as const).map((k) => (
                <td>
                  <Cost cost={game.dailyGift[k][d]} />
                </td>
              ))}
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="gifts">Gifts for a friend</h2>
  <p>
    Any gem pack except the Starter Pack can be bought as a gift for another lord, with a short note. Their gems arrive in their mailbox, and you earn the
    <em>Benefactor</em> emblem.
  </p>

  <h2 id="invites">Inviting friends</h2>
  <p>
    Every lord has an invite code in the game. A friend who enters yours within their first {INVITES.days} days gets <strong>{INVITES.welcomeGems} gems</strong> at once. You
    get gems as they grow: {INVITES.milestones.map((m, i) => <span>{i > 0 && ' and '}<strong>{num(m.gems)}</strong> when their Keep reaches {m.keep}</span>)} — for up to {INVITES.maxFriends} friends. Three friends who
    earned you rewards bring the <em>Recruiter</em> emblem.
  </p>

  <div class="callout blue">
    Something went wrong with a purchase? Open <strong>Settings › About › Write to the team</strong> in the game, or visit <a href="https://nirah.co/legal/support">support</a>. Every
    lord gets an answer.
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .pack {
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .pack h3 {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
  }
  .pack p {
    margin: 2px 0;
  }
  .starter {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }
</style>
